but we all got to work together.

12:03.140 --> 12:05.175
Oh, my God!
Are you drunk again?

12:05.210 --> 12:07.946
Yeah, I was, I was just hanging
out with my main man, Peter.

12:07.982 --> 12:09.550
"Main man"?

12:09.585 --> 12:10.851
"Hanging out"?

12:10.886 --> 12:13.121
Brian, he's only using
you to buy alcohol!

12:13.156 --> 12:14.422
What?
What are, wha...?

12:14.461 --> 12:15.793
What are you,
what are you talking about?

12:15.829 --> 12:17.763
It hasn't dawned on you
that he only started

12:17.798 --> 12:20.001
spending time with you when
the drinking age was raised?

12:20.036 --> 12:21.971
Come on, that's,
that's not true.

12:23.441 --> 12:26.510
Aw, shoot, I puked
in the clean dishes side.

12:26.545 --> 12:28.714
Trust me, as soon as you're
no longer of use to him,

12:28.750 --> 12:29.884
he'll be done with you.

12:29.919 --> 12:31.420
Oh, I get it, I get it.

12:31.455 --> 12:32.856
Okay, you're, you're jealous

12:32.891 --> 12:34.859
'cause I'm spending
all my time with Peter.

12:34.894 --> 12:36.395
Oh, yeah.
Yeah, right.

12:36.430 --> 12:39.165
Yeah, where's my dumb,
morbidly obese friend?

12:39.200 --> 12:40.603
Hey, Stewie, get in here!

12:40.638 --> 12:43.106
I'm being an '80s
computer hacker!

12:43.142 --> 12:46.078
Come on, baby, show
me what you got.

12:46.113 --> 12:48.382
And we... are in!

12:48.418 --> 12:49.719
All right, I'd better go.

12:49.754 --> 12:52.690
I got to go tell him
"This isn't a game, man."

12:52.726 --> 12:54.593
Brian, do you have
any idea why Peter

12:54.629 --> 12:56.062
was trying to climb
in the dishwasher?

12:56.097 --> 12:58.433
I thought it was
a Tokyo apartment.

12:58.468 --> 13:00.235
Sorry, Lois,
we, uh, we got--

13:00.271 --> 13:01.805
I guess we had
a little too much to drink.

13:01.840 --> 13:03.074
"To drink"?!

13:03.109 --> 13:04.812
It's against the law
for him to do that!

13:04.847 --> 13:06.345
Was Stewie in here?

13:06.381 --> 13:09.250
Was, was he in here?
I... I smell his cologne.

13:09.286 --> 13:10.387
Listen to me, Brian.

13:10.422 --> 13:11.955
No more booze in this house.

13:11.990 --> 13:14.093
You're gonna get us
all in trouble.

13:14.128 --> 13:15.895
Peter, we--
maybe we should find

13:15.931 --> 13:17.600
some place else to get--
to drink.

13:17.635 --> 13:19.937
Yeah, I think you're right.

13:21.140 --> 13:23.242
Hi, we're here
from the '80s FBI.

13:23.277 --> 13:25.345
Somebody here
with a 2,400-baud modem

13:25.380 --> 13:26.981
almost started World War III.

13:28.352 --> 13:30.622
Oop, sounds like
they're making an escape.

13:34.529 --> 13:36.364
Hey, you want to see me
run up that slide?

13:36.400 --> 13:38.602
Sure.

13:40.341 --> 13:41.572
Ow, damn it!

13:41.608 --> 13:44.077
I think my belt buckle
cut my gut!

13:44.112 --> 13:46.349
Hey, Peter,
can I ask you something?

13:46.384 --> 13:48.419
You're not just hanging out
with me because I,

13:48.454 --> 13:50.523
I can buy you alcohol, right?

13:50.558 --> 13:52.827
What?! Course not.
We're friends.

13:52.862 --> 13:55.031
Yeah, no, I-I know. That's,
that's, that's what I thought.

13:55.067 --> 13:56.699
And also you bring
me dead birds.

13:56.734 --> 13:58.235
I know Lois gets mad about it,

13:58.271 --> 14:00.373
but I like using them
to point at things.

14:00.408 --> 14:01.941
Hey, did they move the bagels?

14:01.977 --> 14:03.445
Yeah, they're right there.
Oh, my God!

14:03.480 --> 14:04.815
What the hell is that?!

14:04.850 --> 14:07.453
This?
This is a pointing bird.

14:07.488 --> 14:09.053
All right, I just saw
a sprinkler come on,

14:09.089 --> 14:11.091
so I'm gonna go bite
at the water a little bit.

14:12.563 --> 14:14.629
Hey, what's going on here?

14:14.665 --> 14:17.403
Uh, some butthorn's
shining a flashlight on me.

14:17.438 --> 14:19.537
I meant prior to me coming
up and investigating this.

14:19.573 --> 14:21.142
Oh, well, you got
to be clearer, man.

14:21.177 --> 14:22.378
I'm wasted.

14:22.413 --> 14:23.712
Sir, I'm gonna
need to see some I.D.

14:23.748 --> 14:25.316
You look underage.

14:25.351 --> 14:26.484
Just as I suspected.

14:26.519 --> 14:27.552
You're a minor.

14:27.588 --> 14:28.821
It ain't my fault!

14:28.857 --> 14:30.724
Somebody's been buying it
for me and all my friends!

14:30.760 --> 14:31.825
Oh, is that right?

14:31.861 --> 14:33.063
Well, you better
tell me who that is

14:33.098 --> 14:34.330
or you're in a lot of trouble.

14:34.365 --> 14:35.867
Hey, is this the park
where Boner died?

14:35.902 --> 14:37.303
Wait, wha-what's going on?

14:37.339 --> 14:38.538
That's him, Officer!

14:38.573 --> 14:40.074
That's who's been
buying us the booze!

14:40.109 --> 14:41.009
What?!

14:41.045 --> 14:42.379
You get home, son.

14:42.415 --> 14:43.813
You're lucky I'm letting
you off with a warning.

14:43.848 --> 14:45.317
But you, you're coming with me.

14:45.353 --> 14:46.384
You got to be kidding!

14:46.420 --> 14:47.754
Do you need a ride?

14:47.790 --> 14:49.589
Nah, I'm just gonna stay
here until the sun comes up

14:49.625 --> 14:51.960
and then be the
best at tetherball.

14:53.666 --> 14:54.867
Next!

15:00.592 --> 15:02.091
What are you in for?

15:02.127 --> 15:04.729
I bought some alcohol for
someone I thought was my friend.

15:04.765 --> 15:06.099
How about you?

15:06.135 --> 15:08.770
I threw a bottle of rum through
the window of the Apple Store.

15:08.805 --> 15:11.008
I couldn't remember
me password.

15:11.044 --> 15:12.711
Well, this sucks.

15:12.746 --> 15:13.980
Oh, it's not so bad.

15:14.015 --> 15:15.883
Sometimes they let you
take the good trash home

15:15.918 --> 15:17.117
if you ask nice.

15:17.153 --> 15:19.155
Last week, I got
an old greeting card.

15:19.190 --> 15:20.591
It obviously wasn't for me,

15:20.627 --> 15:22.662
but the imagination's
a hell of a thing.

15:24.465 --> 15:25.866
Hey, Brian, what
time you get off?

15:25.902 --> 15:28.137
Me and the guys were hoping you
could buy us some more beer.

15:28.173 --> 15:29.305
You can't be serious.

15:29.340 --> 15:30.641
Eh, it's a little bit serious.

15:30.677 --> 15:31.876
Yeah, I haven't
been drunk in a day.

15:31.912 --> 15:34.113
And I'm not feeling
particularly handsome.

15:34.148 --> 15:35.617
Peter, you're
the reason I'm here!

15:35.653 --> 15:37.520
You totally
sold me out to that cop!

15:37.556 --> 15:39.490
Oh, are we just gonna
play the blame game?

15:39.525 --> 15:41.326
'Cause I got another game
I'd rather play.

15:41.361 --> 15:42.795
Boggle.

15:42.831 --> 15:44.231
Go to hell!
You used me.

15:44.266 --> 15:45.634
That's not what friends do.

15:45.670 --> 15:47.268
It's what Adam Sandler's
friends do.

15:47.304 --> 15:49.773
Now, if you'll excuse me, I've
got a half a can of hot beer

15:49.808 --> 15:52.613
left in this open container
I've been driving around with.

15:58.058 --> 16:00.127
You, too, pig.

16:00.162 --> 16:02.094
Well, I'm not the
smartest man in the world,

16:02.130 --> 16:05.568
but I can always look back on
my life and say I went for it.

16:05.604 --> 16:08.473
Ugh, this seems like a weird
place to even use a condom.

16:08.509 --> 16:10.777
Just shut up, Peter.
I'm done with you, all right?

16:10.813 --> 16:12.781
You completely lied about why
you were hanging out with me.

16:12.817 --> 16:14.015
What?
I never lie.

16:14.050 --> 16:15.952
Well, except for that one time.

16:15.988 --> 16:17.287
Oh, my God!

16:17.322 --> 16:19.358
My husband's having
a heart attack!

16:19.393 --> 16:21.362
Is anyone here a doctor?!

16:21.397 --> 16:23.665
I have a 13-inch penis!

16:25.805 --> 16:27.004
And besides, I'm sick of you

16:27.039 --> 16:28.274
acting like you're
such a victim.

16:28.309 --> 16:29.442
You agreed to buy us booze,

16:29.478 --> 16:30.578
'cause we weren't old enough.

16:30.613 --> 16:31.979
You're not old enough?!

16:32.015 --> 16:33.583
You're a man in his 40s!

16:33.618 --> 16:35.520
This whole law is ridiculous!

16:35.556 --> 16:37.221
Hey, can one of you guys
with elbows

16:37.256 --> 16:39.525
try to get this truck to honk?

16:41.531 --> 16:43.333
Ah, that and giving noogies

16:43.368 --> 16:46.371
is what I miss most
about having elbows.

16:46.407 --> 16:48.741
You know, Brian,
what you said is right.

16:48.777 --> 16:50.379
This law is stupid.

16:50.415 --> 16:51.580
I mean, if it weren't for that,

16:51.615 --> 16:52.950
we never would've
been in this fight.

16:52.985 --> 16:54.686
Yeah, but what difference
does it make?

16:54.720 --> 16:56.789
It's the law.
Nothing we can do about it.

16:56.824 --> 16:58.091
The hell there's not.

16:58.126 --> 16:59.293
I bet if we worked together

16:59.329 --> 17:00.863
we could find a way
to change it back.

17:00.899 --> 17:02.567
I... I don't know, Peter.

17:02.603 --> 17:05.271
Come on, I know it seems hard,
but we can't just give up.

17:05.306 --> 17:07.506
I mean, what if Thomas
Edison had given up?

17:07.544 --> 17:08.710
Uh, what's that?

17:08.745 --> 17:09.844
What's that thing
you're working on?

17:09.879 --> 17:11.114
Well, it's a lightbulb and...

17:11.149 --> 17:12.482
A lightbulb!
Lightbulb!

17:12.517 --> 17:13.718
Yeah, I invented that.

17:13.753 --> 17:15.256
Me-- I'm Thomas Edison.

17:15.291 --> 17:16.523
I invented the lightbulb.

17:16.559 --> 17:17.926
Uh, what's it do?

17:17.961 --> 17:19.695
It lights up a room
using electrical...

17:19.731 --> 17:21.965
Lights up a room using
electrical stuff!

17:22.001 --> 17:25.506
<i>I was about to say that,
because I invented it!</i>

17:25.541 --> 17:26.906
Uh, what are you working on?

17:26.942 --> 17:28.711
It's a phonograph...
Phonograph!

17:28.747 --> 17:30.714
<i>I knew that,
'cause I invented it.</i>

17:30.750 --> 17:32.250
I'm Thomas Edison.

17:32.285 --> 17:33.552
I rule!

17:33.588 --> 17:35.021
♪ Look it up ♪

17:35.056 --> 17:37.627
♪ Edison was a dick. ♪

17:40.467 --> 17:42.433
Okay, Peter, I know how
we can get the law changed.

17:42.468 --> 17:44.338
I've been doing some research,
and it says here

17:44.373 --> 17:47.142
that in eight months, we can
get a non-binding proposition

17:47.177 --> 17:49.980
on the ballot as long
as we get 4,000 signatures.

17:50.015 --> 17:51.683
Ah, screw that,
we're going with plan B--

17:51.718 --> 17:53.554
threaten to kill
the mayor's nephew.

17:53.589 --> 17:55.290
I love you, Dad!

17:55.326 --> 17:56.425
Peter, that's your son.

17:56.460 --> 17:57.592
Shut up, Brian!

17:57.628 --> 17:59.430
He's hugging me!

18:03.139 --> 18:04.705
So, what exactly
is your plan, here?

18:04.740 --> 18:05.975
You'll see.

18:06.011 --> 18:08.379
Just follow my lead.

18:08.414 --> 18:10.416
Ooh, trick-or-treaters!

18:10.452 --> 18:12.085
Well, what do we have here?

18:12.120 --> 18:14.589
A cowboy and a princess?

18:14.624 --> 18:17.660
Uh, yippee-ki-yay, Mr. Mayor.

18:17.698 --> 18:20.834
Oh, a Western princess!

18:20.869 --> 18:22.938
All right, listen, we want
that drinking law gone.

18:22.973 --> 18:25.742
And everybody knows the best way
to get any law struck down

18:25.777 --> 18:27.644
is to get the gays
angry about it.

18:27.680 --> 18:29.414
Bruce?
Jeffrey?

18:29.449 --> 18:30.651
That's right,
Mr. Mayor!

18:30.687 --> 18:32.486
I needs my Proseccos!

18:32.521 --> 18:33.489
What are you talking about?

18:33.524 --> 18:34.657
You're 52.

18:34.693 --> 18:36.994
You said you was 39!

18:37.029 --> 18:38.631
I was just trying
to get you in bed.

18:38.666 --> 18:41.335
I thought we'd both
be dead by now.

18:41.370 --> 18:43.740
Crap. But come on, you got
to change that law!

18:43.776 --> 18:45.476
I mean, it's already
ruined a friendship

18:45.512 --> 18:47.512
with one of the best guys
I know!

18:47.547 --> 18:49.349
Adam, who's at the door?

18:49.384 --> 18:50.552
Oh, hi, Brian.

18:50.586 --> 18:52.020
Hi, Peter.

18:52.055 --> 18:53.323
Wait a minute.

18:53.359 --> 18:55.728
Is that, is that wine?

18:55.763 --> 18:58.732
Yeah, Adam just poured me
a little before dinner.

18:58.767 --> 19:00.033
Wow, you guys eat late.

19:00.068 --> 19:01.103
No, Peter, don't you see?

19:01.138 --> 19:02.671
Carol's underage, too!

19:02.706 --> 19:04.842
The mayor just broke
his own law!

19:04.877 --> 19:07.179
Hmm, that's a good point.

19:07.214 --> 19:09.383
I guess I'll just have
to resign in scandal

19:09.418 --> 19:11.387
while leaving the law intact.

19:11.422 --> 19:14.425
Or you could
just change the law.

19:14.461 --> 19:15.928
But it's a good law.

19:15.963 --> 19:17.130
No, it ain't!

19:17.165 --> 19:18.400
Look, don't you understand
what drinking

19:18.435 --> 19:20.301
means to us working stiffs?

19:20.339 --> 19:21.871
It helps us forget about our day

19:21.906 --> 19:24.209
and tell our children we love
'em with a straight face.

19:24.244 --> 19:27.916
It allows gross uggos to boof
each other's gross uggo parts.

19:27.952 --> 19:30.421
And it gives people the courage
to sneak onto their mayor's

19:30.456 --> 19:33.826
property and blackmail him
and eat all his ripe tomatoes.

19:33.862 --> 19:35.796
That was a croquet ball.

19:35.831 --> 19:39.235
Ah, then could you point me to
the closest nighttime dentist?

19:39.270 --> 19:42.173
So listen, Mr. Mayor,
what do you say about that law?

19:42.208 --> 19:44.443
All right, I'll repeal it.

19:44.478 --> 19:47.214
But only if you send me and
Carol a copy of that picture.

19:47.250 --> 19:50.086
We don't have a lot
of the two of us together.

19:50.121 --> 19:52.590
Brian, we did it!
We got him to change the law!

19:52.626 --> 19:55.095
Just goes to show, if anybody
wants a law changed,

19:55.130 --> 19:57.598
they should just go
to their mayor's house.

19:57.634 --> 19:59.869
Hey, I, uh, I-I appreciate

19:59.905 --> 20:01.706
what you said there
about our friendship.

20:01.742 --> 20:03.277
Well, to be honest, Brian,

20:03.312 --> 20:05.112
at first I did just want you
to buy us beer.

20:05.147 --> 20:07.616
But then the-the more
we were hanging out,

20:07.652 --> 20:10.020
I-I remembered how much fun
we used to have together.

20:10.055 --> 20:11.691
I guess after all these years,

20:11.726 --> 20:13.827
I started taking you
for granted.

20:13.863 --> 20:16.399
But you're still my best friend.

20:16.434 --> 20:18.502
Even if I don't
always act like it.

20:18.537 --> 20:20.271
I enjoyed hanging out
with you, too.

20:20.307 --> 20:22.074
Thanks, Peter.

20:22.109 --> 20:23.979
Hey, on your way out,

20:24.014 --> 20:25.882
could you put this in my
mailbox for the mailman?

20:25.917 --> 20:27.551
Uh, sure.

20:27.587 --> 20:28.987
Put the flag up?

20:29.022 --> 20:30.757
Of course put the flag up!

20:30.792 --> 20:33.162
Geez, mail much?

20:33.386 --> 20:38.389
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru

20:38.572 --> 20:40.541
Well, Peter, I'm just happy
that you and Brian

20:40.576 --> 20:42.209
managed to get
that law repealed,

20:42.244 --> 20:43.712
and that you're
finally friends again.

20:43.747 --> 20:45.147
Me, too, Lois.

20:45.183 --> 20:46.950
Good to have
my drinking buddy back.

20:46.986 --> 20:49.089
Yay, everybody's happy!

20:49.124 --> 20:51.993
I love this family!

20:53.163 --> 20:54.244
I draped that over him.

20:54.245 --> 20:55.946
He was just doing it
out in the open.